Subject: [PATCH 0006] Remove dynamic stack allocation and add a zone census

linuxdoom-1.10 uses alloca in six places.  The SBF backend rejects dynamic
stack allocation outright ("error in backend: Unsupported dynamic stack
allocation" in R_GenerateLookup), so those six sites are the only thing that
stops the engine's translation units from compiling for sbf-solana-solana.
Each one is a short-lived scratch buffer with a single lifetime, so the zone
allocator covers them exactly: Z_Malloc with PU_STATIC, released on every
exit path.  Z_Malloc for a non-purgeable tag cannot purge the caller's own
block, so the allocation sequence the engine observes is unchanged, and the
DEMO1 replay stream is byte-identical afterwards
(DOOM-FB1 2db988a2fa58c294d070fc9e2e6a52de615a8aa4b13ec9af33056985189d69c2,
the retained M463 golden).

Z_Census and the host's --zone-census flag report how much zone the engine
actually holds, which is the number an account-resident arena has to cover.
-mb-used makes the zone size settable so that floor can be probed.  Both are
read-only instrumentation on the host path.

Applies on top of 0001-0005.
